ISO 20022 message schemas
-------------------------
The files in schemas/ are ISO 20022 message schemas (XSD) produced by the
ISO 20022 Registration Authority with its Standards Editor, as published at
https://www.iso20022.org. ISO 20022 is a standard of the International
Organization for Standardization (ISO). They are included unmodified, so that
messages can be validated without downloading anything, and are embedded in
the Iso20022Kit library.

These copies were taken from two Apache-2.0 open-source projects that
redistribute the same files:

  schemas/pacs.008.001.08.xsd
    from mx20022 (https://github.com/socrates8300/mx20022), schemas/pacs/
    SHA-256 9bb360555d1981be8635aa3ed295abfe8b2d221d316193434114ad722107dcde

  schemas/camt.053.001.08.xsd
    from moov-io/iso20022 (https://github.com/moov-io/iso20022),
    docs/specifications/banktocustomer_cash_management_8/
    SHA-256 ca0b135cc8e2dde5b2f99af6b6c514a8f29d6e7c6cf98e9ea84d247189868ff5

Each file's header records how it was generated ("Generated by Standards
Editor (build:R1.6.15) on 2019 Feb 14"). The schemas are subject to the terms
of use of iso20022.org; they are not covered by this project's licence.

The files in src/Iso20022Kit/Generated/ are generated from these schemas by
XmlSchemaClassGenerator (https://github.com/mganss/XmlSchemaClassGenerator,
Apache-2.0); viewer/src/schemas/*.json are generated from them by
tools/SchemaModel.

Data
----
Every message in conformance/ is made up. Bank identifiers such as TSTAKHPP
and DEMOUS33 are fictitious; the two IBANs are the standard documentation
examples GB82WEST12345698765432 and DE89370400440532013000.
